  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$$\n{x}_{1}=9,\\,{x}_{2}=-8,\\,{x}_{3}=-1,\\,{x}_{4}=4,\\,{x}_{5}=2\n$$\n\nGiven the values ${x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4},\\,{x}_{5}$ above, we have\n\n${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}=$ {{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression $1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}$ equals ${x}_{i}$ when ${x}_{i}>0$ and equals $0$ otherwise. Thus, the sum \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i}\n$$\n\nadds up only the positive values.\n\nWe evaluate the indicator function for each ${x}_{i}:$\n\n- $1[{x}_{1}>0]=1[9>0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{2}>0]=1[-8>0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{3}>0]=1[-1>0]=0$\n\n- $1[{x}_{4}>0]=1[4>0]=1$\n\n- $1[{x}_{5}>0]=1[2>0]=1$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1[{x}_{i}>0]\\cdot {x}_{i} & =1\\cdot 9+0\\cdot (-8)+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =9+0+0+4+2 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
